      {
        "id": 203559,
        "name": "cnranger",
        "username": "cnranger",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/53a042/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2017-09-13T16:00:14.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Most people on the forums are probably super fans, myself included. Of course we listen to everything you guys put out. More interludes this month = Awesome!</p><p>However my wife also listens to the podcast occasionally and she skips the interludes even when I tell her they are great with lots of good stuff.</p><p>I asked her why: \"I care more about the characters themselves. 'Interludes' is so vague, I want to learn about Captain Cosmic so why would I listen to something called the interlude?\"</p><p>My follow up: What if it was called Interlude 7: Captian Cosmic? Would you listen to that or expect there to be a Captain Cosmic Episode?</p><p>Her response: \"Maybe. But if you are talking about Captain Cosmic put it in the Captain Cosmic episode. If it was called Interlude 7: EVEN MORE Captian Cosmic. Then maybe yeah.\"</p><p>So she if fully aware of them but believes the content will be uninteresting to her (not character focused) so at least for her its a branding issue. She also rarely listens to the end of the episode and probably misses the \"The next interlude will be about the Dark Watch so send in your questions\" section.</p><p>If you have any additional follow ups I'll gladly ask. Neither of us care about spoilers and listen to them.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
