      {
        "id": 203564,
        "name": "Trajector",
        "username": "Trajector",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/{size}/1914_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-09-14T00:55:13.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I listen to it all, because I’m listening for Sentinels Comics story!</p>\n<p>Along that line, I agree with Spiff that I don’t see the point in calling anything on this podcast a spoiler. However, my reason is different: While we’ve received and been able to piece together a fair amount of story content to go with the game, MOST of this story information is new to us listeners. Why would I get upset to find out some bit of story in the future of the Tactics timeline, but not get upset about the reveal of any other plot beat from the timeline of the card game that we couldn’t have previously known?</p>\n<p>Unless it’s a thing that one of the Tactics scenario books is ABOUT, or a central plot twist to a canonical RPG scenario, I wouldn’t mark anything as a spoiler for story reasons.</p>",
